A||||10||Robert||My second car.......now THAT was a car!||||14||
Z||000000||Robert||02-27-2000||01:22 PM||||My second car was a Nash American, about a 1960 model.  It cost me maybe $150.00, big bucks in those days.  What I didn’t know about the car when I bought it was someone at American Motors dreamed up this great gimmick for this car.  The front seat tilted all the way back to form a full size bed.  Now here I am, a teenager in the height of his sexual powers (it’s been downhill ever since) living in San Francisco in 1967, with 3 drive-ins within 10 miles, and a car that turns into a bed.  Who could ask for anything more?  Not only that, but when I drove up to my dates house in my Nash, the parents didn’t think twice about my intentions, it didn’t carry the stigma of a Van.  Those were the days!!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/amerpump.gif"> <P><p>[This message has been edited by Robert (edited 02-27-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000001||Monkeyman||02-27-2000||02:30 PM||||Unfortunately, my second car was a yellow '75 Gremlin.  I went downhill.  But I had a bunch of really cool cars after that.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierospeeder||02-27-2000||11:21 PM||||my 2nd car was a fiero and still is.  My first was a 74 beetle that didn't run, it needed a new starter.  3rd is my 87 ford thunderbird 2.3l turbo.  Get more respect because less SUVs tailgate you.  <BR>The next 20 cars, i do want to get an AMC pacer.  I think it was garth who got me addicted to it, waynes world.||||reg||1
